+# Findings and limits
+
+The static audit at the recorded revision examined types, Enum boundaries and
+obsolete compatibility behavior after #923/#924/#925 were merged. Compatibility
+preservation was not required. The accepted changes are [#929](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/929)
+(removing three analyzer diagnostic variants with no current producer),
+[#930](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/930) (returning MutationOperator
+from token replacement selection), and [#931](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/931)
+(using ApplyMutation.candidate as the single candidate source). These are
+proposals; this audit does not implement them or demonstrate current CLI failures.[^design-audit-20261016]
+
+The review also checked runtime/session state, report and configuration readers,
+progress, metrics, plan/review boundaries and Python tooling. Current Git and
+Windows fallbacks, useful report projections and optional evidence were not
+classified as obsolete compatibility. The source record explains rejected
+candidates and the boundaries of each accepted change.[^design-audit-20261016]
+
+The scoped philosophy assessment is 7.5/10: six diagnostics supported, locality
+partially unmet, and actual design-investment time unmeasured. Completion needs
+implementation and re-review of the three follow-ups plus time measurements for
+that last diagnostic. Builds, tests, property testing, mutation testing and Lean
+proofs were not run during this audit. Existing tests were inspected to define
+future acceptance criteria.[^design-audit-20261016]
+
